**Analysis:** JWT theft likely due to XSS vulnerability or malicious browser extensions. localStorage accessible to JavaScript, vulnerable to XSS.

**Investigation:**

**1. Check for XSS vulnerabilities:**
```bash
# Review user-generated content endpoints
grep -r "innerHTML" frontend/src/
grep -r "dangerouslySetInnerHTML" frontend/src/

# Check API responses for unescaped content
curl http://api/comments/123
```

Finding: Comment API returns HTML without sanitization, displayed using innerHTML.

**2. Review token storage:**
```javascript
// Current (Vulnerable)
localStorage.setItem('token', jwtToken);
// Accessible via: localStorage.getItem('token')
// Any script can read this
```

**3. Check audit logs:**
```sql
SELECT username, ip_address, user_agent, timestamp
FROM audit_log
WHERE action = 'login'
AND timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '7 days'
ORDER BY username, timestamp;
```

Finding: Multiple logins from different IPs/locations for same users.

**Immediate Mitigation:**

**1. Invalidate all existing tokens:**
```java
@Service
public class TokenInvalidationService {
  @Autowired
  private RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate;

  public void invalidateAllTokens() {
    // Add all issued tokens to blacklist
    String currentTime = String.valueOf(System.currentTimeMillis());
    redisTemplate.opsForValue().set("token:global:invalidation", currentTime);
  }

  public boolean isTokenValid(String token) {
    Claims claims = parseToken(token);
    String globalInvalidation = redisTemplate.opsForValue()
      .get("token:global:invalidation");

    if (globalInvalidation != null) {
      long invalidationTime = Long.parseLong(globalInvalidation);
      long tokenIssuedAt = claims.getIssuedAt().getTime();

      if (tokenIssuedAt < invalidationTime) {
        return false; // Token issued before invalidation
      }
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

**2. Force re-authentication:**
```java
@PostMapping("/auth/force-logout")
public void forceLogoutAll() {
  tokenInvalidationService.invalidateAllTokens();
  // Send email to all users about security incident
  userService.sendSecurityAlert();
